{
  "_readme": "Every image is a SPRITE SHEET (a grid of frames) or a background. Drop the ChatGPT image into assets/img with exactly this file name and run: python3 tools/process_art.py. It keys out the magenta, slices the grid (cols x rows), shrinks every frame to 'cell' pixels (real pixel art), snaps colours to the shared palette and aligns the frames ('bottom' = feet on one baseline, 'center' = centred). The game draws everything at 2x with no smoothing. What each frame means: src/sprites.js. Missing files show as placeholder blocks.",
